@map/sandbox "Game master sandbox"
" An empty map with nothing in it but the player ships - no enemies, no stations,
" no terrain. A Game Master builds the scenario live from the Game Master console:
" Spawn places ships, fleets, stations, players and terrain wherever it is pointed.
" To end the game, use the Game Master console: Commands, then end game.
metadata:``` yaml
Properties:
  Main:
    Player Ships: 'gui_int_slider("$text:int;low: 1.0;high:8.0;", var= "PLAYER_COUNT")'
    Difficulty: 'gui_int_slider("$text:int;low: 1.0;high:11.0;", var= "DIFFICULTY")'
  Map:
    Time Limit: 'gui_input("desc: Minutes;", var="GAME_TIME_LIMIT")'
```
# The map settings are deliberately NOT offered here (issue #576). Terrain, Lethal
# Terrain, Friendly Ships and Monsters only feed a map's opening spawn, and this map has
# none. Upgrades and Seed went the same way: a setup screen for a map the Game Master
# builds by hand should ask for the two things that are still decided up front - how many
# player ships, and how long the game runs - and nothing else. Both settings keep whatever
# settings.yaml gives them, so a mission that wants them can still set them there.

    #------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    # EMPTY BY DESIGN. Nothing is spawned here beyond the player ships - the Game Master
    # populates the map during play. This map has never spawned stations or friendlies
    # (they were commented out in the commit that created it); the description used to
    # promise them anyway, which is what #576 reported.
    await task_schedule(spawn_players)
    # Player ships share scan data with each other (an extra_scan_source link each way).
    await task_schedule(default_player_friendly_eyes)
    # Registers the docking logic rather than docking anything now - it is what makes the
    # stations the GM spawns LATER dockable. Not dead code, despite the empty map.
    await task_schedule(docking_standard_player_station)

    #------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
